 "text": "Hi, how you doing right now? Then go backwards through time. Start with modern history and work your way up to classics like The Rise and Fall of the Roman Empire. Yes, start with ancient Rome. It' the root of modern history. Mostly about big events, so it' not the most page-turning read. But it' fascinating how much of it still applies today. Try a short history of the world in a thousand years. It gives a great overview in a few hours. You'll find the short one is often based on same events, just squeezed into half the time.",
